{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_specs_2026_08_18_responsive_export_design", "label": "Responsive Export Design", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-18-responsive-export-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_responsive_css_injection", "label": "RESPONSIVE_CSS Injection Mechanism", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A single shared RESPONSIVE_CSS <style> block (duplicated independently in Python and JS since the two HTML-assembly paths don't share code) injected into every page the app emits: a blanket @media (max-width:768px) rule collapses any inline grid-template-columns to 1fr, safe for virtually all real grid layouts.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-18-responsive-export-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_data_wd_stack_optin", "label": "data-wd-stack Opt-In Attribute", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "HTML attribute opt-in marking exactly the flex-row wrapper elements that should stack to flex-direction:column on mobile, since most display:flex usage in the block library is small inline UI groups that should stay row at any width; ships as infrastructure only, no block currently needs it.", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-18-responsive-export-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_html_assembly_functions", "label": "Shared HTML-Assembly Injection Points", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The four page HTML-assembly functions (backend _project_to_html and _build_project_bundle; frontend buildStandaloneHtml and buildCleanExport) are the shared touch-point set repeatedly extended: custom_js (codepen-editor) and RESPONSIVE_CSS (responsive-export) are both spliced into the same four points.", "source_file"